WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.098
HKDSE 2026, Paper 1, Question 10. Topic: Stem-and-Leaf: Quartiles, Range & Probability. This is the full worked solution in English.

2
00:00:12.518 --> 00:00:19.453
The stem-and-leaf diagram below shows the distribution of the numbers of driving hours of a group of taxi drivers in a week.

3
00:00:19.613 --> 00:00:36.369
Stem (tens) Leaf (units) 2 5 6 9 3 2 3 3 6 6 7 8 4 0 0 2 2 5 5 7 7 7 5 w The ratio of the range to the inter-quartile range of the distribution is 7:3. (a) Find w.

4
00:00:36.529 --> 00:00:39.939
(i) Write down the mode of the distribution.

5
00:00:40.099 --> 00:00:44.605
(ii) If two taxi drivers are randomly selected from the group.

6
00:00:44.765 --> 00:00:50.816
find the probability that the mean of their numbers of driving hours in the week exceeds the mode of the distribution.

7
00:00:51.236 --> 00:00:59.466
STEP 1 — list the 21 values (with w equals 3, max equals 53).

8
00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:12.868
Key rule: Range of a Data Set. range equals largest value - smallest value. The largest value is 50 plus w and the smallest is 25, so the range is 25 plus w.

9
00:01:13.028 --> 00:01:42.119
25, 26, 29, 32, 33, 33, 36, 36, 37, 38, 40, 40, 42, 42, 45, 45, 45, 47, 47, 47, (50 plus w). The smallest value is 25, so the range is (50 plus w)-25 equals 25 plus w.

10
00:01:42.539 --> 00:01:47.420
STEP 2 — find the quartiles.

11
00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:57.460
Key rule: Quartiles of an Ordered Data Set. Q sub 1 equals median of the lower half, Q sub 3 equals median of the upper half.

12
00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:07.174
With n equals 21 the median is the 11 th value 40, and Q sub 1 equals 33, Q sub 3 equals 45.

13
00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:21.059
n equals 21, so the median is the 11th value equals 40. Q sub 1 equals mean of the 5th and 6th values of the lower half equals (33 plus 33) over 2 equals 33.

14
00:02:21.219 --> 00:02:37.397
Q sub 3 equals mean of the 5th and 6th values of the upper half equals (45 plus 45) over 2 equals 45. IQR equals Q sub 3 minus Q sub 1 equals 45 minus 33 equals 12.

15
00:02:37.817 --> 00:02:43.488
Step 3. PART (a) — use the ratio 7: 3.

16
00:02:43.648 --> 00:02:55.183
Range over IQR equals 7 over 3 which gives 25 plus w over 12 equals 7 over 3 25 plus w equals 28 which gives w equals 3.

17
00:02:55.603 --> 00:03:00.413
Step 4. PART (b)(i) — mode.

18
00:03:00.573 --> 00:03:09.867
Both 45 and 47 appear three times (the highest frequency), so the distribution is bimodal: the modes are 45 and 47.

19
00:03:10.287 --> 00:03:15.639
Step 5. PART (b)(ii) — probability.

20
00:03:15.799 --> 00:03:24.336
Key rule: Probability with Equally Likely Outcomes. P(E) equals n(E) over n(S).

21
00:03:24.496 --> 00:03:33.460
Only 8 pairs out of to the power 21 C sub 2 equals 210 have a sum above 94, giving 4 over 105.

22
00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:43.064
Total ways to choose 2 drivers: to the power 21 C sub 2 equals 210. Let the two values be x and y.

23
00:03:43.224 --> 00:03:51.799
we need x plus y is greater than 2 times 47 equals 94 (the mean exceeds the mode, i.e. exceeds both modes).

24
00:03:51.959 --> 00:04:07.114
Only pairs containing 53 can qualify (47 plus 47 equals 94 is not is greater than 94): 53 with 42, 45 or 47: 1 times (2 plus 3 plus 3) equals 8 pairs.

25
00:04:07.274 --> 00:04:12.511
P equals 8 over 210 equals 4 over 105.

26
00:04:12.931 --> 00:04:28.994
So the answer is: (a) w equals 3 (b)(i) 45 and 47 (bimodal) (b)(ii) P equals 4 over 105 (exceeding both modes; 11 over 105 if "mode" means 45).

27
00:04:29.414 --> 00:04:38.293
That completes HKDSE 2026 Paper 1 Question 10. Every step shown here matches the worked solution on the page.
